    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia**_\n\nTwo small additions to `sp-ai-load` from the closed #269 (the rest of #269 is already in `main`):\n\n- A second call reports \"already loaded\" instead of loading again, and a failing `sp-ai` load raises a `user-error`.\n- It waits for Elpaca (`elpaca-wait`), so the packages and MCP servers are usable when the command returns (also from `emacsclient -s mcp -e '(sp-ai-load)'`). `sp-terminal` is still loaded first.\n\nThe docs note in `sp-ai.org` is updated to match. Checked only that `init.el` reads cleanly in Emacs 31.1; I did not run a full start-up. No CHANGELOG edit (nightly routine owns it).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
    "changed_files": 2,
